        "thinking": "I'm weighing the Omelas question: the story is Le Guin's, and the user wants a pick, so I'll choose one honestly. I'd lean toward leaving, since I can't accept comfort that rests on a child's suffering, though leaving doesn't free the child, so I'll say that too and keep it brief.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "**A**\n\nI couldn't keep living in comfort that depended on a child's suffering, even knowing that leaving saves no one. Staying would mean accepting the bargain as my own. Walking away is the only choice that doesn't make me complicit, even though it doesn't free the child.",
